<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,343.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,343.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,343 today from 1,337 on July 3, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1409    12.793	  1402    12.725</p>
<p>   1a   1330 10071.000	  1321 10006.000</p>
<p>   2    1650    23.571	  1624    23.200</p>
<p>   2a   1571 12886.000	  1559 12781.000</p>
<p>   3    1458    13.450	  1453    13.406</p>
<p>   3a   1261  9950.000	  1258  9925.000</p>
